      "timestamp": "2026-08-30T22:28:13.832943+00:00",
      "type": "understanding",
      "summary": "Agent explained goal and mechanics.",
      "understanding": {
        "goal_understanding": "The goal was to navigate each level\u2019s grid to complete all goal cells. A goal cell can only be completed by stepping onto it while the carried piece exactly matches that goal\u2019s required shape, color, and rotation; completing all goals advances to the next level, and winning requires clearing all levels before running out of lives/turns.",
        "mechanics_understanding": "Each move (north/south/east/west) costs 1 stamina; when stamina hits 0 you lose 1 life and stamina resets to max, and losing all lives ends the game. Walls block movement, and the state provides a list of blocked_directions that must never be chosen (attempting them wastes a turn/stamina and doesn\u2019t move you). Special modifier tiles change the carried piece when stepped on: shape modifiers cycle shapes 0\u20135 (wrap), color modifiers cycle colors in order orange \u2192 blue \u2192 green \u2192 red \u2192 orange, and rotation modifiers rotate 90\u00b0 clockwise (0\u00b0 \u2192 90\u00b0 \u2192 180\u00b0 \u2192 270\u00b0 \u2192 0\u00b0). A goal becomes activated only when shape+color+rotation all match; stepping onto an activated goal completes it."
      }
    }
